    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d374-a4">

                <pb facs="0692" n="630" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg630"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Report.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Finance</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1878-09-17"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 17,
                    1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In the opinion of the section, the coupon treated of in the preceding note
                    belongs to the false bonds issued by Woodhouse, and not to the genuine bonds put
                    in circulation by Gen. José’ Maria de Jesus Carbajal, the house of Corlies &amp;
                    Co., of New York, being commissioned for their printing and sale, since the
                    former appears to be emitted for 41,000, and the denominations of the latter are
                    exclusively of $50, $100, and $500. In the first is expressed the period
                    extending from the 1st of March to the 1st of September, 1874, while from the
                    legitimate Carbajal bonds only those coupons were cut off corresponding to the
                    two half-years included between October 1, 1865, and the same date of 1866. The
                    figures on the white ground indicating the value of the coupon are larger on the
                    one examined than on those belonging to the said Carbajal bonds; and, lastly,
                    the latter is identical with another coupon formerly received as false, which is
                    found in one of the volumes of the respective report.</p>
                <p>With the foregoing the secretary believes it has given the report asked of it in
                    the border of to-day.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName>Mexico</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1878-09-17">September 17,
                        1878</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>FRANCO. RAMIREZ CASTAÑEDA</signed> (a rubric),<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Third Official.</hi></closer>
            </div>
